    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40665" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπταίρω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sneeze at</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υἱός μοι
				ἐπέπταρε πᾶσιν ἔπεσσιν</span> he <i>sneezed</i> as I
			spoke the words (a good omen), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.545
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				297
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				7.107
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>to be gracious to, favour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρωτές τινι ἐπέπταρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					7.96
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαθός τις ἐ. ἐρχομένῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18.16
				</span></i>
			.</div>
